3. How to Place Shapes & Bridge with Quintic PH Curves

• Placing the Crosses or Stars: Center a small, fixed-size repeatable vector ornament (such as a diamond glyph or four-point cross) directly on each of the six \((X, Y)\) coordinates. Because the step intervals \(\Delta Y\) narrow gradually from 115 down to 64, the chain of ornaments naturally conveys perspective and deceleration.
• Connecting with Quintic PH Segments: Bridge each consecutive pair of markers—such as \((0, 0) \to (125, 115)\)—with a standalone quintic PH curve. Because each bridge is only 125 units wide and stays strictly inside the first quadrant, you can lock all quadratic weights \(u_i, v_i > 0\) to guarantee zero cusps and zero flipping tails across the entire composition.
